#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Lifecycle of one agdev installation: inspectable, resumable, scoped to it.

`agdevctl --config <instance.toml> <command>` (help: `agdevctl --help`), with the Python
standard library (3.11+), outside the replaceable runtime. On Linux it runs as root
(sudo): it administers the Docker dependencies and the native core's systemd units, and
runs everything else under the installation's service accounts. On macOS it runs as the
one user whose LaunchAgents are the installation's services. Gitea is either the
installation's own (Docker) or an existing service it attaches to ([dependencies]).
Host facts come from the config; secrets live in <root>/config/secrets (mode 0600)
and are never printed. See docs/install.md.
"""
